cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GasBench in your research, please cite the companion paper as follows."
title: "GasBench: A Reproducible Benchmark for Drift-Aware Gas Sensor Recognition"
abstract: >-
  GasBench packages the evaluation protocol behind calibration-guided domain
  adaptation (CGDA) for gas sensors: three public datasets, six protocol
  families (LOBO, budget, chronological, single-source, open-set, concentration
  transfer, domain/event detection), eight training mechanisms, and a
  standardized, hashed, reproducible reporting contract.
authors:
  - family-names: Peng
    given-names: Jingyi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
date-released: "2026-09-15"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - gas sensors
  - sensor drift
  - domain adaptation
  - open-set recognition
  - anomaly detection
  - benchmark
